      <h1 style="font-size:clamp(2rem,4vw,3rem);line-height:1.15;margin-bottom:1.25rem;">Understanding Anxiety: Why Your Body Thinks You Are in Danger</h1>
      <p style="font-family:'Lora',Georgia,serif;font-size:1.05rem;color:rgba(220,215,201,0.8);line-height:1.85;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Anxiety is not a character flaw. It is not weakness. It is your nervous system doing exactly what it was designed to do, just at the wrong time, in the wrong place, and far more often than it needs to.</p>
